Z||000000||saleenfiero||09-18-2000||05:41 PM||||Is there any body out there who knows or have done a targa style roof conversion?  Kinda like a t-top only with no T bar in the middle I think it would look kick ass and am well aware of the need to brace the chassis.  In a few words, what would the procdure be?  It would be a sunny day car only with no immediate need for a top of sorts.||||reg||1
Z||000001||contra||09-18-2000||11:42 PM||||this is what i want to do to my fiero as well<BR>as far as i'm guessing i would need to xframe my fiero i think...just to give it strength from collapsing in the middle.<BR>i have a gt, so i would cut along the winshield area, and the line that the fastback meets the roof part.<BR>somehow i would have to figure out how to latch the roof onto the body, i've never done any sort of big mods like this so i havent looked into it yet. but i'm sure i would need some sort of locking latch.<BR>i would need to reinforce the windows i think cause they rattle like a B*tch when they're half down, imagine if the roof was gone. hehehehe<P>it'll be something i'll think about in the longer run of my fiero's life<BR>and may also never happen  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>oh well<BR>good luck<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||09-19-2000||03:00 AM||||X brace the frame. YES reinforce the windows NO. It would be just like a t-top car as far as the windows are concerened. And you could make the latching and sealing just like the t-top cars just one panel instead of two. Pretty simple. If I had one to play with that I didnt have to drive everyday I could make it work. Any body wanna leave there car with me for a bit?||||reg||1
